//! A BYTES AT A TEXT SEAT IS THOSE BYTES VIEWED AS TEXT, through the
//! one door that hands a Bytes to a text row: an extern over the
//! runtime's own symbol. A row's seat kind is `Ptr`, which a string
//! and a `Bytes` both fill — natively one headered box, read the same
//! way — so the engines answer the same text. The decode is lossless
//! for UTF-8: a snowman round-trips, and a NUL inside neither shortens
//! nor ends the text.
extern fn avra_str_trim(b: Bytes) -> string

"${avra_str_trim(" hi ".bytes())} ${avra_str_trim(" hi ".bytes()).length} ${avra_str_trim("☃".bytes())} ${avra_str_trim([104, 0, 105].bytes()!).length}"
